@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:ceaa000d8f9e569975f761aa3e072b48487c43d7 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It now opens with the thing a Rust developer recognises: a dependency pinned to an exact version, a lock held across an await, a test that builds its own fixture." }
~ Open with the thing a Rust developer recognises: a dependency pinned to an exact version, a lock held across …

It now opens with the thing a Rust developer recognises: a dependency pinned to an exact version, a lock held across an await, a test that builds its own fixture. Each was a decision resting on something true at the time, none of it in the code, and some of it in a commit message that cannot be queried and never says when the ground under it moved.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:ceaa000d8f9e569975f761aa3e072b48487c43d7 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Then what the tool does, shown rather than described, with real output from this repository:" }
~ Show what the tool does rather than describe it.

Then what the tool does, shown rather than described, with real output from this repository: one commit read back with its rejected alternative beside it, and `stale` naming the functions that have changed under recorded reasoning.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": "Answering \"why is this like this?\" was dropped as a product claim." }
~ Drop the claim of answering 'why is this like this?' as a product feature.

Answering "why is this like this?" was dropped as a product claim.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The tool assigns labels, sources and statuses; the model proposes wording only." }
~ Assign labels, sources and statuses; the model proposes wording only.

The tool assigns labels, sources and statuses; the model proposes wording only. Every quote is checked against the commit, and an absent quote caps its unit at `speculative`.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Staleness by item body hash. }
~ Detect staleness by item body hash rather than line ranges.

Staleness is attached to code identity rather than to line ranges, so a function that moved is not stale and one that changed is.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Review as records. }
~ Record review as confirmations, withdrawals with reasons, and closures with notes.

Review as records. Confirming writes an attestation, rejecting writes a withdrawal whose reason unit says why, closing writes a resolution. The log keeps everything.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": It ships its own instrument. }
~ Ship its own instrument for benchmarking the model.

It ships its own instrument. `bench` measures the model *you* chose on *your* commits, and every published figure names the model it came from — including four experiments that failed and are listed so nobody repeats them.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Two thirds of the commands never call a model. }
~ Focus on deterministic commands over model-dependent ones.

Two thirds of the commands never call a model. Those are the ones worth your time today: they are deterministic, tested, and cost nothing to run.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The figures are published, naming the model each came from, including the experiments that failed." }
~ Publish figures naming the model each came from, including failed experiments.

The figures are published, naming the model each came from, including the experiments that failed. The rest of this document is that account — written for someone deciding whether to spend an afternoon on this, and reviewing the tool as it was built rather than as it was designed.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Over-production is the failure mode that matters. }
~ Highlight over-production as the failure mode that matters.

Over-production is the failure mode that matters. A corpus of 54 decisions for a four-decision commit is worse than no corpus, and prompt wording was measured twice as not being the lever.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The hook only queues and `--estimate` prices a run before it starts. }
~ Meaningfully price extraction runs before starting them.

The hook only queues and `--estimate` prices a run before it starts.

@decision d/gceaa000d8f9e-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@ceaa000d8f9e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A cloned corpus is someone else's claim. }
~ Label cloned corpora as someone else's claims.

A cloned corpus is someone else's claim. Units carry the status the tool gave them; read `speculative` as what it says.

